OPTION 1 — Easiest & Recommended: Use MetalLB

MetalLB provides LoadBalancer support for bare-metal/local clusters.

Install MetalLB:
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/metallb/metallb/v0.13.10/config/manifests/metallb-native.yaml

Create an IP address pool:

Pick an unused IP range from your LAN or VirtualBox network, e.g.:

192.168.56.240 - 192.168.56.250


Create the config:

apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: IPAddressPool
metadata:
  name: default-pool
  namespace: metallb-system
spec:
  addresses:
    - 192.168.56.240-192.168.56.250
---
apiVersion: metallb.io/v1beta1
kind: L2Advertisement
metadata:
  name: default
  namespace: metallb-system


Apply it:

kubectl apply -f metallb-config.yaml


Then check:

kubectl get svc -n ingress-nginx


You will now see a valid EXTERNAL-IP:

ingress-nginx-controller  LoadBalancer  192.168.56.240


Your DNS can point to this IP.
